WEBVTT

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.190
Onee-sama?

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.630
Onee-sama?!

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.800
Is something wrong, Yumi?

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.340
Calling out so loudly like that.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.280
Onee-sama, where had you gone?

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.710
I'm sorry. There was a store over
there that had caught my eye.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.850
I see, and that was why...

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.020
I was so sure...

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.460
Yumi, what's the matter?

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.960
Is it so trying for you to be on this date with me?

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:40.900
No...

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.370
No, I just lack confidence...

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.810
Like just now, I thought you had
become disgusted with our date...

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.840
...and gone home...

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.420
How silly of you.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.350
That would never happen.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:58.720
I am...

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.160
Onee-sama...

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.530
That reminds me...

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.410
Didn't you just say that a certain
store had caught your eye?

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:25.040
Oh, it was that store over there.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:26.080
Huh?

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.540
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.320
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.190
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.170
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.560
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.830
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.410
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.220
Maria Watches Over Us

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.900
Good Day, Onee-sama

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.440
Pedestrians
Bicycles
ONLY

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.410
Pedestrians
Bicycles
ONLY
Honestly!

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.280
Tanuma Chisato-san was
being so overly friendly!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.180
She's only Rei-chan's date for half a day!

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.450
And Rei-chan is part of the problem, too!

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.020
How can she smile and look so delighted?!

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.820
The sky is so blue, and yet... What am I doing?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.800
This is a precious day off.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.660
I have to enjoy it in my own way.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.170
Pedestrians
Bicycles
ONLY

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.370
Life is a green light.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.640
I don't have time to be jealous
and come to a standstill.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.510
Go, go, Yoshino.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.080
Go for it Yoshino!

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.590
It was unexpected that there was no microwave,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.200
but overall, it was a delicious lunch.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.060
So...

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.740
How much have you figured out about me?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.180
Let me think...

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.340
I have yet to get a clear picture.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:50.740
Why is it?

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:55.850
I feel as though Shizuka-sama
can see right through me.

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.360
Even though I've told her nothing.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.760
Even though I haven't laid my heart bare.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.160
We still have time, don't we?

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:06.930
Yes...

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:09.690
Just for today,

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.000
let's both forget about things like
outward appearances and standing.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:13.700
What?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:15.910
Follow me.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.010
Shizuka-sama?!

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.030
Shizuka-sama, why?

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.710
Never disturbing the pleats of your skirt,

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.000
never running in hallways...

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.970
I wanted to see the you beneath
the mask of the model student.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:57.150
That white card on Valentine's
Day was your heart.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:01.050
You have to hide it,

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:04.420
but at the same time, you wish for it to be found.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.390
For someone to understand.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.330
Am I wrong?

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:14.030
I'm sorry.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.900
For doing something akin to
trespassing upon your heart.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:19.900
You must hate me now.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:24.340
No, I like you, Shizuka-sama.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.520
Words spoken when one is surprised
come close to the truth...

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:34.890
Would it be right for me to take it that way?

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.250
Tell me, Yumi...

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.330
Yes?

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:47.830
With so many here, how do you find
the pair of jeans that you want?

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.730
I am beginning to feel less confident about this.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:55.370
So my Onee-sama has never
been to a jeans shop, either.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.110
But why did she suddenly
become interested in jeans?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.280
This is where I have to be strong.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.110
Yumi?

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.810
Please do not worry, Onee-sama.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.880
I am with you.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.060
Thank you. That's so reassuring.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:16.400
First, we needn't look at the
shelves beyond this point,

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.460
since those are menswear.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:18.360
I see.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:22.330
Thus, our work in looking around
has been halved all at once.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:23.430
You have a good point.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.330
Next comes color,

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:28.180
but since this will be your first pair,

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.800
why not go with a standard pair of blue jeans?

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:32.640
What are yours?

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.180
Pardon?

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.180
I want the same thing that you have.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:36.980
What?

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:41.420
Because it was seeing you that
made me want a pair of jeans.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:46.320
That was why I could not help but
be drawn to this shop earlier.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.450
I'm sorry to have worried you.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.560
Onee-sama...

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:55.470
It was her kind desire to have a
pair that was the same as mine?

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.540
Now, please call me once you
have changed into them.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.940
We will adjust the length.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.000
All right.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.010
Then, I will get changed.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:12.750
Oh... my...

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.020
I wonder if she's doing okay...

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.290
O-Onee-sama...

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.730
Was it not to your liking, after all?

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:24.700
That isn't it.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.820
Yumi, is this right?

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.560
P-Please excuse me.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.500
Everyone must have long legs.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:37.440
Oh, no, they make these long to start with.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:41.310
They always have to cut off
this much for me every time.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:42.670
They do?

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:45.250
Yes, I will adjust the length now.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.860
It suits you very well, Onee-sama.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:52.260
Really?

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.120
Yes!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:58.690
Say, Yumi.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:08:59.590
Yes?

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.590
I know what store I want to go to next.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:04.900
Onee-sama?

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.240
New Lord of Monster:
A Certain Love

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:07.680
Higashimachi Odewon Theatre

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.380
Higashimachi Odewon Theatre
Shoot...

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:08.810
Shoot...

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.510
I guess the start times for the next screenings...

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:15.950
...aren't the same as the end
times of the previous screenings...

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:21.180
In other words, Rosa Foetida en
bouton and Tanuma Chisato-san...

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.720
...have long since left the theater...

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:25.360
I am so sorry.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.420
It's fine. I didn't realize it, either.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.350
Now, chin up.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.170
Let us switch our target to white now.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.800
To Shimako-san and Shizuka-sama?

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:40.170
They bought take-out food,

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:43.300
so they must be having lunch
at a park or something.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.710
Come, we are going to hit every park in the city!

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:47.850
I shall accompany you.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:51.750
How ironic.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:55.550
If Rosa Gigantea didn't exist,

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:58.490
we may have become soeurs.

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:02.260
But Rosa Gigantea does exist.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.760
And we love her greatly.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.260
That is why we are happy, isn't it?

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.840
Do you like "Ave Maria"?

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.910
Yes, Gounod's especially.

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.770
Then I shall perform it for you.

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:22.810
What?

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.310
In part, to thank you for today.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.780
Maria Watches Over Us

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.450
Welcome back.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.780
Your stuff was here,
so I figured you'd be coming back.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.680
Why?

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:20.260
Shizuka asked me to come, but I've
found you instead for some reason.

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:24.090
Onee-sama...

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.460
I...

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.500
I missed you.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.570
I'm right here.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:53.430
What is it, Yumi? You have
such a silly smile on your face.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:57.860
Oh, no, it just makes me so happy
to think we have matching jeans.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:02.740
The truth is, when I came dressed like this,

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:06.430
I was worried about what to do if I did
not match how you were dressed.

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:11.150
You know, in the past, I used
to doggedly try on my own...

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:14.110
...to change the parts of me that
differed from everybody else.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:19.520
I was so determined since the time
I started kindergarten at Lillian.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:23.250
I stopped being driven to
and from in a private car,

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.950
changed my lunch,

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.630
tried watching TV shows...

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.930
...that the majority of my
classmates were watching...

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:32.130
There was even a time I got myself
so worked up that I became ill.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:35.770
What is the matter with me?

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:38.540
Bringing up the past like that.

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:42.680
I would like to hear more
about your past, Onee-sama.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.400
Oh, of course, not just about the past.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.820
Then, shall we talk about the present?

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:52.140
And a little bit of the future?

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:55.210
About the future?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.430
Yoshino-san!

00:14:58.960 --> 00:14:59.690
Yumi-san.

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.620
Good afternoon, Sachiko-sama.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.690
Good afternoon, Yoshino-chan.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.290
Are you out shopping?

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:07.900
Yes...

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:09.970
Or rather, I wish I could say that,

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.100
but the truth is, I was anxious about
Rei-chan and Tanuma Chisato-san.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:15.730
Yoshino-chan...

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.740
But I am over it now.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.940
After all, it isn't like me to get
all twisted up with jealousy.

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:28.410
Yoshino-chan, if you would like,
would you care to join us for tea?

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:31.580
But won't I be intruding?

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:35.280
Not at all. The more the merrier.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:36.660
Right, Yumi?

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:37.560
Yes.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.360
There's actually a cafГ© that I've
wanted to go to for a while.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:51.740
Sachiko-sama... Yumi-san... and Yoshino-san!

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.670
Oh, this is just too bad!

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:59.080
Tsutako-san, what happened to your camera?

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:02.560
Shortly after we came in,
someone from the store came up to us...

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:06.190
...and warned me, "Please don't
take pictures in the store."

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:10.020
I had intended to get the
scoop on the boutons' dates,

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:13.160
but I'm going to forget about
the school paper for today.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.130
You're giving up with unusually good grace.

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:18.730
Today, I'm just tired...

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:21.670
...and besides, the cake here is very delicious.

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.240
You're right, it's delicious.

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.080
Oh, your cheesecake looks
nice too, Yoshino-san.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:27.980
May I have a little?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.140
Here you are.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.220
The tea is wonderfully fragrant, too.

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:37.910
And even after that, Minako-sama
said not a word about the paper,

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:40.890
Tsutako-san never once took her camera out,

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:45.530
and Yoshino-san never once mentioned Rei-chan.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:47.070
By the way,

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:50.630
the chocolate chiffon cake that I
ordered was also really delicious.

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:55.640
This unexpected tea party that concluded
my date with Sachiko-sama...

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.940
...felt to me like a very luxurious time.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.180
Pardon me for losing control.

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:09.890
If you wish it,
I'll keep you company until morning.

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:11.820
Oh no...

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.250
Crying might be a good sign.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:18.690
You should show more vulnerability,
as befitting your age.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:23.870
If you take it upon yourself to
bear it all, you'll be crushed.

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:28.900
I'm sure no one would fault you if
you showed some vulnerability.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.440
Yes...

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:34.570
But I cannot bring myself to take that next step.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:36.640
Spring will come soon.

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.210
Will things change with the coming of spring?

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.650
Sure. Cherry blossoms will flower.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.350
New people will come into your life.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.130
The spring that brought you to me, Onee-sama.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:52.430
Right, the spring that
brought you to me, Shimako.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:04.310
You know, Yoshino-san,

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:08.950
Rei-sama was truly kind and I felt so lucky.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.680
Uh, um, Chisato-san...

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:13.740
What are you doing here?

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.390
Rei-chan's house is next door, you know...

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.380
But...

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.560
Without realizing it, Rei-sama...

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:25.620
...called me "Yoshino" five times.

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:34.200
No matter what we were talking about,
no matter where we were,

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:36.710
you were there inside Rei-sama...

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:44.650
I'm sorry.

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:47.720
I'm so sorry.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.320
I'm sorry my big sister is so insensitive.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:55.920
So there you have it.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.430
You're to blame!

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:03.830
You're the most to blame!

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.160
Yoshino...

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:13.410
You're just too nice to girls to begin with!

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.710
For all that you're really, really nice,

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:18.940
in exchange, you end up
hurting people in little ways.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:21.980
I'm sorry.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:26.520
I'm so sorry, Yoshino.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:30.060
Yoshino,
I'm sorry for today.

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.360
Hello, is this the Ogasawara-san residence?

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:37.200
I'm a high school student
at Lillian Girls' Academy...

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.870
...in Year 1, Peach Class and
my name is Fukuzawa Yumi.

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:42.680
I apologize for disturbing you at night,

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:45.880
but I would appreciate it if I might
speak to Sachiko-sama on the phone.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.950
All right, rehearsal was perfect.

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:51.490
Oh, is it weird that I use
"san" for Ogasawara-san,

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:54.150
but use "sama" for Sachiko-sama?

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.580
Then, do I say "Ogasawara-sama's residence"?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:01.720
I want to call my Onee-sama
to thank her for today,

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:04.100
but I have no idea who
might answer the phone...

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:06.000
I'm having a hard time placing the call...

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:11.840
Y-Yes? Fukuzawa residence.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:14.370
I apologize for disturbing you at night.

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:16.880
I'm a high school student
at Lillian Girls' Academy...

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.010
...in Year 2 and my name is Ogasawara...

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:19.000
Onee-sama?!

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:21.240
Oh, thank goodness! Is that you, Yumi?

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:26.950
Yes, I was just thinking of
calling you at home as well.

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:28.410
So it seems.

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.350
You answered after one ring, so I can tell.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:34.790
Um, thank you very much for today.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:40.190
In all honesty, I was a little nervous
about calling your house.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.240
I was worried about whether
I could greet them properly...

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.640
...if either your mother or
father answered the phone.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.300
After all, I have no idea what
you have told them about me.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:53.580
I've told them that you are a
wonderful big sister, of course.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:55.040
Really?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.610
Are you sure you haven't said that
I am a spoiled and hysteric big sister?

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:00.140
Only a little.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:01.050
Hey!

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:09.360
You're heavy.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:25.510
I had such fun.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.150
Let's go out together again.

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:28.410
Yes!

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:32.980
Oh, yes... About the future
that she had mentioned...

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:34.350
Well then, Yumi,

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:37.260
good night and I will see you tomorrow.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.620
Yes, good night.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.460
"See you tomorrow."

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:51.190
Tomorrow, I will get to see my
beloved Onee-sama again.

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:55.670
Because today was such an enjoyable day,

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:59.540
tomorrow will undoubtedly
be another wonderful day!

00:22:00.550 --> 00:22:01.450
And that's...

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.610
...the future awaiting my Onee-sama and I.

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:09.150
Good night, Onee-sama.

00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:12.690
See you tomorrow.
